  <page>
    <exercise>
      <title>Section 3.2 - Multiple Linear Regression</title>

      <introduction>
        <p>
          This question involves the use of multiple linear regression on the
          <xref ref="day01-Auto-csv"/>.
          It is a modified version of Problem 3.7.9 in the textbook.
          Using the <sq>Auto</sq> data set, we will predict
          <m>Y = \texttt{mpg}</m> using all other variables except <c>name</c>
          and <c>origin</c>.
          (11 points)
        </p>
      </introduction>

      <task xml:id="hw02-P3-7-9-a">
        <statement>
          <p>
            Generate the correlation matrix between all variables.
            Are there any pairs that are particularly highly correlated?
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>

      <task xml:id="hw03-P2-7-9-b">
        <statement>
          <p>
            Using <sq>statsmodel</sq>, create a linear model predicting
            <c>mpg</c> from all other variables except <c>name</c> and
            <c>origin</c>.
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>

      <task xml:id="hw02-P3-7-9-c" worskpace="1in">
        <statement>
          <p>
            Is there a relationship between the predictors and the response?
            Justify your answer.
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>

      <task xml:id="hw02-P3-7-9-d" worskpace="1in">
        <statement>
          <p>
            Which predictors appear to have a statistically significant
            relationship to the response?
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>

      <task xml:id="hw02-P3-7-9-e" worskpace="1in">
        <statement>
          <p>
            What does the coefficient for the year variable suggest?
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>
    </exercise>
